From: Gleb Pesin <dormancygrace@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] osdrv: build without W=1 warnings

The drivers build with -Werror, so make W=1 failed: 43 warnings in the code and 11
missing include directories.

- Makefiles: drop include directories that do not exist (sys, cif, ive,
  cvi_vc_drv). LDDINCDIR is never set, so "-I$(LDDINCDIR)" was a bare -I
  that took the next flag as a directory: -DCNM_FPGA_PLATFORM (vcodec),
  -DCHIP_BM1880 (jpeg) and -Wno-date-time (cvi_vc_drv) never reached the
  compiler. The two defines are dropped with it, so the code stays as
  built; nothing in these modules tests them. -Wno-date-time now applies.
- Variables that were set but never read are removed. Where only disabled
  code (VC_DRIVER_TEST, CVIDEBUG_V, REDUNDENT_CODE, !CONFIG_SUSPEND) reads
  one, it is marked __maybe_unused instead.
- LogMsg and jdi_LogMsg take printf formats; with __printf the compiler
  checks their callers, and the 64-bit addresses printed with %x, %lx, %d
  or %p now use %llx, and pointers use %p.
- vb_print_pool: strncat with the whole buffer size could write past the
  64-byte line; it now uses snprintf and strlcat.

Machine code changes only in vb_qbuf (no longer calls sys_get_chipid for
an unused value), vb_print_pool and DecRegisterFrameBuffer (no longer
computes an unused buffer size). Everything else differs only in line
number and string offset constants.

